{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mira_valenhart","name":"Mira Valenhart","role":"protagonist","description":"A seventeen-year-old apprentice cartographer at Silverspine Academy, Mira is small, ink-stained, and sharp-eyed, with wind-tangled auburn hair she ties back with surveying twine. Raised by a mapmaker aunt after her parents vanished on a failed bridge crossing, she has memorised the drift patterns of every isle but has never left Silverspine's charts to see the bridges up close.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To make sure no other family is lost the way her parents were when a skybridge frayed without warning.","goal":"Survey and repair the failing skybridges before the isles drift beyond reach of one another.","flaw":"She trusts her charts over people and dismisses advice that contradicts her measurements.","internal_conflict":"She longs to prove herself as a true cartographer yet fears that her maps are what failed her parents.","external_conflict":"The Toll War closes the bridges she needs to survey, and Cartel agents block her access to the most damaged spans.","arc":"Mira begins as a chart-bound apprentice who trusts only her own measurements. When the Toll War shuts the Mistral Docks lanes, she must rely on a Hollow Circle miller's wind-lore to reach a failing span, and discovers her charts were wrong about the drift. She ends as a cartographer who combines maps with the knowledge of others and leads a joint repair crew.","personality_traits":["curious","stubborn","meticulous","guilt-ridden"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Charting","description":"Predicts how islands and skybridge tension will shift by reading wind patterns and survey data.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cloudstone Surveying","description":"Spots hairline fractures and fraying in cloudstone cables using calibrated tools.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_torren_ashgrip","name":"Torren Ashgrip","role":"supporting","description":"A broad, soot-faced master braider at Emberroost in his fifties, Torren has burn-scarred forearms and a booming laugh. He learned the old cable-braiding techniques from the generation that remembered the First Weaving, and he guards them closely within the Bridge Wardens.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the craft of cloudstone braiding alive after the last of his master's generation has died.","goal":"Braid a replacement cable strong enough to anchor the most strained skybridge.","flaw":"He hoards his techniques and refuses to write them down or teach outsiders.","internal_conflict":"He fears dying with the craft unpassed but cannot bring himself to trust anyone with it.","external_conflict":"Cartel tolls have starved Emberroost of cloudstone shipments, leaving him short of material.","arc":"Torren starts as a secretive craftsman who works alone in his shielded forge-pit. When a shortage of cloudstone forces him to rely on Mira's survey data to use scraps efficiently, he shares his braiding method with her and her crew. He ends as a teacher who trains a new generation of braiders.","personality_traits":["gruff","proud","generous with food","secretive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Master Braiding","description":"Weaves cloudstone strands into load-bearing skybridge cables within a shielded forge-pit.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Forge-Pit Discipline","description":"Works heat and metal safely inside shielded pits, never exposing open flame aloft.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_valdis_crowe","name":"Valdis Crowe","role":"antagonist","description":"A polished, silver-haired merchant prince of the Drift Cartel in his forties, Valdis wears a coat stitched with trade-lane insignia and speaks softly. He rose through the Cartel after the signing of its charter and treats the skybridge tolls as his family's legacy.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's dominance over inter-isle trade so his family never again depends on others.","goal":"Raise skybridge tolls and bring all crossings under Cartel control.","flaw":"He measures everything by profit and cannot see value in what cannot be sold.","internal_conflict":"He privately knows the bridges are failing but fears that admitting it would collapse the trade he built.","external_conflict":"The Wardens oppose his tolls while the Hollow Circle resists his grain levy, and Mira's repairs threaten his leverage.","arc":"Valdis begins as a confident toll-master who hides the extent of the bridges' decay. When a Cartel cargo barge is stranded after a span nearly gives way, he must face Mira's evidence of the failure. He ends by suspending the toll increase and funding repairs, accepting a smaller but lasting share of trade.","personality_traits":["calculating","charming","ruthless","image-conscious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane Control","description":"Directs Cartel shipping lanes and bargains with captains to shape trade across the isles.","category":"social"},{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Persuades rivals and officials with smooth negotiation and well-timed concessions.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_fallowmere","name":"Oren Fallowmere","role":"supporting","description":"An elderly miller of The Hollow with a weathered face, white whiskers, and a stooped back, Oren lived through the memory of the Great Calm as told by his grandmother. He can read the wind by the creak of his windmill sails and speaks in short, plain sentences.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect the Hollow's grain-growers from being ruined by the Cartel's levy.","goal":"Keep grain flowing to the isles without paying the Cartel levy.","flaw":"He distrusts anyone from outside the Hollow and refuses help even when it would save his people.","internal_conflict":"He values the Hollow's independence yet knows it cannot survive without the bridges others maintain.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy forces the Hollow Circle to choose between paying the Cartel or losing its markets.","arc":"Oren begins as a wary miller who turns away outsiders. When Mira arrives stranded by the Toll War and needs wind-lore to reach a failing span, he guides her, and sees that the bridges that carry his grain are worth defending. He ends as a Hollow Circle envoy who works with the Wardens.","personality_traits":["taciturn","wise","suspicious","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind Reading","description":"Forecasts gusts, calms, and storms from the sound and movement of windmill sails.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sable_quill","name":"Sable Quill","role":"supporting","description":"A lean, quick-witted deck pilot at Mistral Docks in her early twenties, Sable has cropped dark hair and a patched flight coat. She ferries cargo and passengers across the isles on a small wind-skiff and knows every shortcut around Cartel toll-gates.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To earn enough to buy her own skiff and escape her debt to the Cartel.","goal":"Pay off her accrued wind-debt and fly independently.","flaw":"She takes reckless shortcuts and breaks promises when a better deal appears.","internal_conflict":"She wants freedom from the Cartel but fears she is nothing without its trade lanes.","external_conflict":"Her wind-debt has come due, and Valdis's agents threaten to seize her skiff.","arc":"Sable starts as a Cartel-bound pilot chasing quick profit. When she is hired to smuggle Mira past a closed toll-gate and a storm nearly destroys her skiff, she chooses to stay and ferry repair materials instead of fleeing with the payment. She ends as a free pilot who repays her wind-debt through labour for the Wardens.","personality_traits":["bold","witty","impulsive","loyal once committed"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skiff Piloting","description":"Flies a small wind-skiff through crosswinds and narrow gaps between islands and skybridges.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Toll-Gate Knowledge","description":"Knows the schedules and blind spots of Cartel toll-gates across the archipelago.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mira_torren_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_torren_ashgrip","target_character_id":"chr_mira_valenhart","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Torren Ashgrip reluctantly mentors Mira Valenhart in cable braiding, but his secrecy about his techniques strains their partnership."},{"id":"rel_mira_valdis_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_valdis_crowe","target_character_id":"chr_mira_valenhart","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Valdis Crowe obstructs Mira Valenhart's surveys and tolls her crossings because her proof of failing bridges threatens his hold on trade."},{"id":"rel_mira_oren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_mira_valenhart","target_character_id":"chr_oren_fallowmere","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mira Valenhart earns the trust of Oren Fallowmere, who shares wind-lore with her in exchange for her pledge to protect the bridges that carry Hollow grain."},{"id":"rel_sable_mira_ally","source_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","target_character_id":"chr_mira_valenhart","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sable Quill ferries Mira Valenhart past Cartel toll-gates for pay, and the partnership grows into genuine loyalty."},{"id":"rel_valdis_sable_rival","source_character_id":"chr_valdis_crowe","target_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Valdis Crowe holds Sable Quill's wind-debt over her and threatens to seize her skiff when she helps Mira Valenhart."},{"id":"rel_valdis_oren_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_valdis_crowe","target_character_id":"chr_oren_fallowmere","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Valdis Crowe imposes the Grain Levy on Oren Fallowmere's Hollow Circle, and Oren refuses to pay it."}]}
