{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_isolde_marrow","name":"Isolde Marrow","description":"A lean, wind-weathered courier in her thirties who carries sealed parcels across the skybridges between isles. She grew up in the cramped dock-quarters of Mistral Docks, wears a patched grey flightcoat, and keeps a brass cartographer's compass inherited from her mother. She has crossed more bridges than almost anyone alive and carries a heavy ledger of wind-debt.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To clear the wind-debt her late mother left her and win a life that is not owned by the Cartel.","goal":"Decode the strange sealed message she was handed and deliver its meaning to the people who can understand the builders of the skybridges.","flaw":"Chronic self-reliance that makes her hide dangerous information rather than share it.","internal_conflict":"She wants freedom from the Cartel but fears that without its protection she is nothing more than a debtor adrift.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants the message suppressed because it could upend its toll-based hold on the bridges.","arc":"Isolde begins as a lone courier who hoards secrets to stay safe. When Cartel agents demand the message at Mistral Docks and Corvin offers to help instead, she chooses to share the full message with the Wardens at Silverspine rather than sell it. She ends trusting allies and openly breaking with the Cartel, her debt bought out by the community she helped.","personality_traits":["resourceful","guarded","wry","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Navigation","description":"Knows the shifting bridge routes and wind currents by instinct, crossing quickly and safely.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Pattern Reading","description":"Spots recurring patterns in cloudstone weave marks, helping to decode the message.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_ashgrove","name":"Corvin Ashgrove","description":"A stooped, ink-stained senior cartographer at Silverspine Academy, in his sixties, with silver-white hair and spectacles mended with copper wire. He has spent decades charting the skybridge network and privately suspects its design follows an older, deliberate plan.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that the skybridge network was laid out by a deliberate design, vindicating a lifetime of mocked research.","goal":"Obtain and translate the message so the Academy accepts his theory about the network's builders.","flaw":"Pride that makes him dismiss help from people without scholarly credentials.","internal_conflict":"He yearns for recognition yet fears the truth might show his life's work was built on a misreading.","external_conflict":"The Academy council refuses to fund his research, and Cartel interference threatens any attempt to examine the message.","arc":"Corvin starts as a proud scholar who scorns non-academics. When Isolde shows him pattern marks he missed in the cloudstone weave, he admits his error and credits her publicly. He ends as a humbler collaborator who values her field knowledge over credentials.","personality_traits":["erudite","stubborn","curious","absent-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Network Cartography","description":"Reads and reconstructs the evolving map of the skybridge network.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Archive Lore","description":"Draws on Academy records to cross-reference weave patterns and ancient notations.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_brannoch_vale","name":"Brannoch Vale","description":"A broad-shouldered, soot-streaked Bridge Warden master braider at Emberroost, in his fifties, with burn scars on his forearms from the shielded forge-pits. He is known for his gruff manner and his unshakable devotion to bridge safety.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep every skybridge safe and protect the apprentices who braid them from the Cartel's escalating tolls.","goal":"Use the message's engineering knowledge to strengthen the bridges and break the Cartel's toll leverage.","flaw":"Distrust of outsiders that leads him to turn away useful allies.","internal_conflict":"He values safety above all but suspects that guarding the old ways may be holding the Wardens back.","external_conflict":"The Toll War leaves the Wardens underfunded while the Cartel raises crossing costs.","arc":"Brannoch starts as a rigid guardian who refuses outside help. When a cable frays during the Toll War and Isolde's route knowledge saves an apprentice crew, he accepts her aid. He ends by opening the Warden forge to the new techniques in the message.","personality_traits":["gruff","loyal","methodical","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Braids load-bearing skybridge cable inside shielded forge-pits, observing the ban on open flame.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Structural Assessment","description":"Judges a bridge's strength by touch and sound.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_sera_dunmoor","name":"Sera Dunmoor","description":"A sharp-eyed, impeccably dressed Drift Cartel factor at Mistral Docks, in her forties, who wears rings of polished basalt and keeps meticulous ledgers of every debt owed in the archipelago. She was Isolde's patron after her mother's death.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To protect the Cartel's monopoly on trade, which she believes keeps the isles fed and orderly.","goal":"Seize the message and suppress it before it can undermine Cartel toll authority.","flaw":"Controlling nature that treats people as ledger entries and cannot accept loss of leverage.","internal_conflict":"She genuinely cares for Isolde like family yet sees her only as a debt to be collected.","external_conflict":"The Toll War and Grain Levy disputes are eroding Cartel support, making the message a threat she must contain.","arc":"Sera starts as Isolde's controlling patron who values leverage over people. When Isolde defies her at Mistral Docks and the Hollow Circle refuses the grain levy, her leverage collapses. She ends isolated but forced to renegotiate tolls, leaving her to weigh whether to keep her control or accept her place among equals.","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","ambitious","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Brokering","description":"Uses wind-debt obligations to compel loyalty and extract favors.","category":"social"},{"name":"Ledger Memory","description":"Recalls every debt and transaction across the archipelago.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_orchard","name":"Tamsin Orchard","description":"A cheerful, weather-tanned Hollow Circle miller in her twenties, with flour-dusted braids and strong arms, who runs a windmill that grinds grain for half the archipelago. She has never left The Hollow before the story begins.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep her community fed and free from the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Secure a fair shipping route that bypasses the levy and carry her harvest safely to the isles.","flaw":"Naive trust that makes her vulnerable to Cartel manipulation.","internal_conflict":"She fears leaving home but knows her people's survival depends on someone speaking for them.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy imposed by the Drift Cartel threatens her mill's survival.","arc":"Tamsin starts as a sheltered miller who trusts authority and fears the bridges. When Sera's agents try to exploit her trust in the levy dispute, she crosses the skybridges with Isolde as her guide to testify to the Wardens. She ends as a confident voice for the Hollow Circle.","personality_traits":["warm","earnest","hardworking","timid"],"abilities":[{"name":"Milling Expertise","description":"Runs windmills efficiently and judges grain quality at a glance.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Community Rapport","description":"Easily earns the trust of farmers and millers.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_sera_isolde_patron","source_character_id":"chr_sera_dunmoor","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_marrow","relationship_type":"patron","description":"Sera Dunmoor holds Isolde Marrow's wind-debt and acts as her patron, a tie of affection and control that becomes conflict when Sera demands the message."},{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_ally","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrove","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Marrow brings the sealed message to Corvin Ashgrove, who decodes it with her; their partnership begins in mutual suspicion over credentials and field knowledge."},{"id":"rel_brannoch_sera_rival","source_character_id":"chr_brannoch_vale","target_character_id":"chr_sera_dunmoor","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Brannoch Vale opposes Sera Dunmoor over the Cartel's rising skybridge tolls in the Toll War, each blaming the other for the strain on the bridges."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_isolde_friend","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orchard","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_marrow","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Tamsin Orchard relies on Isolde Marrow as her guide across the skybridges, and their friendship grows as Isolde learns to share her burdens."},{"id":"rel_sera_tamsin_adversary","source_character_id":"chr_sera_dunmoor","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orchard","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Sera Dunmoor enforces the Grain Levy against Tamsin Orchard's mill and tries to exploit her trust, driving the Hollow Circle's resistance."}]}
