es a small brass lantern shield for use only in approved forge-pits.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To earn enough to protect his family's mill from the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Send his full salvage share home before the levy deadline.","flaw":"He is reckless in trying to prove himself.","internal_conflict":"He wants to be seen as capable but is terrified of the dark corridors.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy threatens his family while the liner's presence lures him deeper into its halls.","arc":"Tobin begins as an eager rookie who hides his fear behind bravado. Lured by whispers in the fog-filled ballroom, he wanders off alone and is nearly lost until Mara pulls him back. He ends humbler, admitting fear and relying on the crew's help.","personality_traits":["eager","earnest","impulsive","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Nimble Climber","description":"Moves quickly across rigging and broken decking.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_crane","name":"Isolde Crane","description":"A silver-haired Silverspine cartographer in her sixties, hired by the crew to chart the liner's drift path. Precise and austere, she wears ink-stained gloves and keeps a ledger of sightings of the lost ship. Her late husband was a passenger when it vanished.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To learn what happened to her husband aboard the liner.","goal":"Find the passenger manifest and the captain's log.","flaw":"Obsessive curiosity makes her ignore warnings.","internal_conflict":"She wants the truth yet fears it will confirm he suffered.","external_conflict":"Mara wants to leave quickly with the cargo while the ship's presences guard the records.","arc":"Isolde starts as a detached scholar who insists on staying in the officers' deck. After reading the log in the fog-shrouded bridge and finding her husband's name, she is tempted to 