es a small brass lantern shield for use only in approved forge-pits.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To earn enough to protect his family's mill from the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Send his full salvage share home before the levy deadline.","flaw":"He is reckless in trying to prove himself.","internal_conflict":"He wants to be seen as capable but is terrified of the dark corridors.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy threatens his family while the liner's presence lures him deeper into its halls.","arc":"Tobin begins as an eager rookie who hides his fear behind bravado. Lured by whispers in the fog-filled ballroom, he wanders off alone and is nearly lost until Mara pulls him back. He ends humbler, admitting fear and relying on the crew's help.","personality_traits":["eager","earnest","impulsive","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Nimble Climber","description":"Moves quickly across rigging and broken decking.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_crane","name":"Isolde Crane","description":"A silver-haired Silverspine cartographer in her sixties, hired by the crew to chart the liner's drift path. Precise and austere, she wears ink-stained gloves and keeps a ledger of sightings of the lost ship. Her late husband was a passenger when it vanished.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To learn what happened to her husband aboard the liner.","goal":"Find the passenger manifest and the captain's log.","flaw":"Obsessive curiosity makes her ignore warnings.","internal_conflict":"She wants the truth yet fears it will confirm he suffered.","external_conflict":"Mara wants to leave quickly with the cargo while the ship's presences guard the records.","arc":"Isolde starts as a detached scholar who insists on staying in the officers' deck. After reading the log in the fog-shrouded bridge and finding her husband's name, she is tempted to remain with the ship. She chooses to leave with the crew and carry the record home, accepting his loss.","personality_traits":["meticulous","austere","curious","grieving"],"abilities":[{"name":"Chartwork","description":"Reconstructs drift paths and ship layouts from fragments of maps.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_the_purser","name":"The Purser","description":"The ghostly steward of the liner, a tall figure in a salt-stained uniform with a hollow gaze, perpetually offering welcome to guests. It has kept the ship's fog-wreathed halls in order for decades and cannot let any passenger disembark.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep every guest aboard so the voyage never ends.","goal":"Bind the salvage crew to the ship as new passengers.","flaw":"It cannot bend its rigid hospitality rules.","internal_conflict":"It clings to duty yet faintly remembers the night it failed its passengers.","external_conflict":"Mara's crew is determined to leave and take the ship's belongings with them.","arc":"The Purser begins as a courteous warden sealing the exits with fog. When Mara gives up the strongbox and Isolde returns the manifest, the ritual of hospitality is fulfilled in a way it cannot refuse. It lets the crew depart and its presence fades, ending its duty.","personality_traits":["courteous","unyielding","mournful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fog Binding","description":"Thickens the fog to disorient and seal passages.","category":"supernatural"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tobin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_ash","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Mara Voss is Tobin Ash's captain and reluctant mentor, but her reliance on his labour pushes him into danger."},{"id":"rel_isolde_mara","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_crane","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Isolde Crane clashes with Mara Voss, since 