oost, with soot-stained gloves and braids pinned under a leather cap. She oversees cloudstone cable braiding and has seen the toll revenue fail to reach bridge repairs.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe for everyone, after a frayed cable killed a colleague under her watch.","goal":"Prove that Cartel tolls are being diverted from repairs, and secure funds for her failing cables.","flaw":"Obsessive perfectionism that makes her blame herself and hesitate to act without complete proof.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between loyalty to the Wardens' neutrality oath and the need to take a political side to save the bridges.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's rising tolls strain her budget, and her superiors forbid Wardens from entering politics.","arc":"Starts as a cautious engineer who refuses to leak anything without airtight proof. When a cable fails during a storm and nearly drops a crossing, she gives Marcellus the repair logs showing diverted toll money, even though it breaks her oath. She ends as a witness before the senate, accepting imperfect certainty in order to protect lives.","personality_traits":["meticulous","guilt-ridden","dedicated","observant","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and inspecting skybridge cables inside shielded forge-pits.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Structural Assessment","description":"Can judge a bridge's failing points by sound and tension.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_seraphine_drosk","name":"Seraphine Drosk","description":"A poised Cartel princess in her fifties, with silver rings and a ledger-bound coat, who runs shipping lanes from Mistral Docks. She bankrolled Crass's rise as an investment and keeps a calm, courteous manner that hides her calculation.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's monopoly over inter-isle trade by installing a pliable ruler.","goal":"Keep Crass in power and under her control while discrediting Marcellus Vane.","flaw":"Contempt for ordinary people leads her to underestimate their capacity to resist.","internal_conflict":"She values stability and order yet knows Crass's volatility threatens the system she built.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy provokes the Hollow Circle, and Marcellus's investigation threatens to expose her payments to Crass.","arc":"Starts as a confident patron who views Crass as a controllable asset. When the Hollow Circle's resistance and Marcellus's confession start to unravel public trust, she attempts to quietly buy Marcellus's silence and then abandons Crass to protect the Cartel's charter. She ends having preserved her wealth but lost her political puppet, forced to negotiate with those she once dismissed.","personality_traits":["composed","calculating","patient","condescending","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Shipping Leverage","description":"Can delay or redirect cargo across the archipelago to pressure rivals.","category":"social"},{"name":"Debt Brokering","description":"Uses wind-debt obligations to bind people to her interests.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_vane_crass_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_marcellus_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tiberon_crass","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Marcellus Vane is determined to expose Tiberon Crass as a Cartel puppet, while Crass uses Marcellus's disgrace as proof that the senate is corrupt."},{"id":"rel_crass_drosk_patron","source_character_id":"chr_seraphine_drosk","target_character_id":"chr_tiberon_crass","relationship_type":"patron","description":"Seraphine Drosk funds and directs Tiberon Crass's campaign, expecting him to deliver the Cartel's goals, while Crass chafes at her control."},{"id":"rel_halloway_vane_ally","source_character_id":"chr_wren_halloway","target_character_id":"chr_marcellus_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Wren Halloway distrusts Marcellus Vane but agrees to a tentative alliance after he publicly confesses, linking the Hollow Circle to his campaign against Crass."},{"id":"rel_fenwick_vane_informant","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_fenwick","target_character_id":"chr_marcellus_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Fenwick secretly supplies Marcellus Vane with bridge repair logs, risking her Warden oath to prove that Cartel toll money is being diverted."},{"id":"rel_drosk_halloway_rival","source_character_id":"chr_seraphine_drosk","target_character_id":"chr_wren_halloway","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Seraphine Drosk imposes the Grain Levy while Wren Halloway organizes the Hollow Circle against it, making them direct opponents over the island's grain."}]}
