:"A broad-shouldered, soft-spoken Bridge Warden engineer in his fifties with burn scars on his forearms from shielded forge-pits. Trained at Emberroost, he now surveys the failing skybridge anchors at the edge of the glass wastes, carrying braided cloudstone cable and a worn survey staff.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges standing so no traveller is stranded as he once was.","goal":"Repair the failing anchor at the edge of the glass expanse before the season turns.","flaw":"He over-promises repairs he lacks the resources to complete.","internal_conflict":"He resents the Wardens' rules yet feels guilty for every bridge he cannot save.","external_conflict":"Cartel tolls starve the Wardens of funds and cable, so he must repair anchors with scavenged materials.","arc":"Begins as a Warden who hides how badly his repairs are failing. When Isolde crosses and her weight exposes a flaw in his anchor, he must admit the truth to her rather than bluff. He ends by openly asking the Hollow Circle and travellers for labour, accepting shared effort over solitary pride.","personality_traits":["gentle","dutiful","tired","honest-when-pressed"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable braiding","description":"He braids cloudstone cable with exceptional speed and strength.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Anchor sense","description":"He can feel through his staff when a bridge anchor is weakening.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_dask","name":"Corvin Dask","role":"antagonist","description":"A polished, hawk-faced Cartel factor in his forties with ink-stained gloves and a coat trimmed in silver thread. Based at Mistral Docks, he enforces levies and collects wind-debts on behalf of the merchant princes, tracking debtors with meticulous ledgers.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure a seat among the merchant princes by collecting every outstanding debt.","goal":"Intercept Isolde's ledger, which contains evidence of falsified Cartel toll records.","flaw":"Obsessive need to be seen as irreproachable, which makes him ruthless to hide mistakes.","internal_conflict":"He privately knows the tolls are unjust but fears losing status if he questions them.","external_conflict":"The Toll War and the Grain Levy dispute put him at odds with the Wardens and Hollow Circle, who resist his collections.","arc":"Begins as a loyal factor who enforces tolls without question. He confronts Isolde at the glass-bridge edge and, seeing the falsified records himself, must choose between burying them or exposing the Cartel. He chooses to bury them and is left isolated, having protected his position at the cost of the integrity he once claimed.","personality_traits":["meticulous","charming","calculating","insecure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt tracking","description":"He can trace any traveller's wind-debt through Cartel ledgers and informants.","category":"social"},{"name":"Negotiation","description":"He persuades or pressures merchants into favourable terms.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_corvin_isolde_pursuit","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_dask","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Dask pursues Isolde Vane to seize the ledger she carries and to collect her family's grain levy debt, driving the central conflict of her crossing."},{"id":"rel_taren_isolde_aid","source_character_id":"chr_taren_holt","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Taren Holt aids Isolde Vane with water and a safe route across the glass, challenging her refusal of help and adding to her wind-debt."},{"id":"rel_corvin_taren_toll","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_dask","target_character_id":"chr_taren_holt","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Corvin Dask's rising tolls strain Taren Holt's repair funds, setting the Cartel against the Bridge Wardens in