{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_venn","name":"Mara Venn","description":"A lean, soot-streaked Bridge Warden engineer in her thirties from Emberroost, with burn-scarred forearms from years braiding cloudstone cable in shielded forge-pits. She lost her brother when a skybridge failed during the Toll War, and she carries his cracked copper measuring-callipers everywhere. She is blunt and exacting, and she trusts only what she has tested herself.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To make sure no one dies on a neglected skybridge the way her brother did.","goal":"Expose and repair the sabotaged transit-bridge junction before the archipelago's main skybridge grid collapses.","flaw":"Contemptuous of anyone who has not worked with their hands, so she dismisses allies who could help her.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect everyone but blames herself for not inspecting her brother's bridge in time.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls starve the Wardens of repair funds while the sabotaged grid fails around her.","arc":"Starts as a lone, distrustful engineer who dismisses outsiders. When a crossing of the sabotaged Mistral span strands her with Cartel pilot Joren Kaul, she has to accept his shipping knowledge to reroute the grid. She ends by leading a joint Warden-Cartel repair crew, having learned to share responsibility instead of carrying it alone.","personality_traits":["blunt","meticulous","guilt-ridden","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and splicing cloudstone cable under tension, working only in shielded forge-pits.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Load Sense","description":"Can judge a skybridge's stress and fatigue by feel and sound.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_joren_kaul","name":"Joren Kaul","description":"A charming, weathered skiff pilot in his forties who works the shipping lanes out of Mistral Docks for the Drift Cartel. He wears a salt-stained captain's coat with a cartel signet ring he is quietly ashamed of. He knows every wind current and every back-lane between the isles.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To pay off his family's mounting wind-debt and keep his crew employed.","goal":"Keep his shipping lanes open through the crisis without breaking his Cartel contract.","flaw":"Chronic people-pleaser who tells each side what it wants to hear.","internal_conflict":"He is loyal to the Cartel that feeds his family but sickened by what its tolls do to ordinary isles.","external_conflict":"Cartel master Isolde Brask demands he divert cargo to profiteering runs while the grid fails.","arc":"Starts as a smooth, noncommittal Cartel loyalist. Stranded on the failing Mistral span with Mara, he must choose between obeying Isolde's order to abandon the stranded and flying them out. He chooses to rescue them, openly defies the Cartel, and ends as a committed ally who finally stands for something.","personality_traits":["charming","evasive","resourceful","guilt-prone"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windreading","description":"Reads wind currents and plots safe flight lines between isles.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Smooth Talk","description":"Negotiates with dockhands, wardens and merchants alike.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_brask","name":"Isolde Brask","description":"A silver-haired Cartel merchant princess in her sixties who runs the Drift Cartel's toll offices from Mistral Docks. Her rings are each stamped with a clause of the Cartel Charter. She is composed, courteous and ruthless, convinced that order flows from controlled trade.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To make the Cartel's hold on inter-isle trade permanent and unchallengeable.","goal":"Use the grid crisis to impose a Cartel-run toll authority over every skybridge.","flaw":"Believes everything and everyone has a price, so she fatally underestimates principled people.","internal_conflict":"She sees herself as the archipelago's stabiliser but knows her policies deepen its suffering.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist her tolls and her grain levy, threatening to unite against her.","arc":"Starts as a confident monopolist exploiting the crisis. When Joren defies her and the Wardens and Hollow Circle refuse her levy together, her leverage collapses. She ends stripped of the toll authority, forced to accept a shared charter and facing the cost of her own certainty.","personality_traits":["composed","calculating","patient","imperious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Mastery","description":"Tracks debts and wind-debt obligations across the whole archipelago.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Leverage Network","description":"Commands loyalty through the debts she holds over captains and merchants.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_harrow","name":"Tobin Harrow","description":"A broad, soft-spoken Hollow Circle miller in his fifties with flour-dusted hands and a bad knee, from The Hollow. He survived the Great Calm as a boy and remembers the hunger. He is the trusted voice of the farming isle's windmill cooperatives.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep the archipelago fed and his people free from the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Organise the Hollow Circle to withhold grain from the levy and open independent shipments through the repaired bridges.","flaw":"Avoids confrontation and hoards his doubts until they become crises.","internal_conflict":"He wants to stay neutral and safe but knows neutrality starves his neighbours.","external_conflict":"Isolde's Cartel levy threatens to strip The Hollow's granaries during the crisis.","arc":"Starts as a quiet miller who avoids taking sides. When the Cartel levy leaves The Hollow's granaries nearly empty, he travels to Emberroost and stands with Mara before the Wardens. He ends as an outspoken leader who commits the Hollow Circle to the alliance.","personality_traits":["gentle","patient","wary","resilient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Sense","description":"Judges harvest quality, storage and supply needs across isles.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Community Trust","description":"Farmers across several isles listen to him.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_lysa_orrin","name":"Lysa Orrin","description":"A young cartographer-scholar at Silverspine Academy, slight and ink-stained, with a habit of sketching maps on her sleeves. She is brilliant but sheltered, having studied skybridge charts far more than she has crossed them.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that charting the drift can predict and prevent bridge failures.","goal":"Trace the sabotage by matching altered bridge charts to the failed junctions.","flaw":"Naive and overconfident in her models, she ignores field evidence that contradicts them.","internal_conflict":"She yearns to do real work in the field but fears her theories will fail when tested.","external_conflict":"Academy elders and the Cartel pressure her to keep the altered charts quiet.","arc":"Starts as a theory-bound scholar who trusts her models over people. After her predicted-safe route fails and Mara's field inspection proves her wrong, she works beside Mara. She ends by publishing the tampered charts that expose the sabotage, having learned to test theory against reality.","personality_traits":["brilliant","earnest","sheltered","curious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Charting","description":"Models the shifting skybridge network and predicts drift patterns.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_joren_uneasy_allies","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_joren_kaul","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Venn and Joren Kaul begin as wary adversaries, Warden against Cartel pilot, and grow into allies as they survive the Mistral span together."},{"id":"rel_isolde_joren_master","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_brask","target_character_id":"chr_joren_kaul","relationship_type":"employer","description":"Isolde Brask holds Joren Kaul's family wind-debt and orders him to profiteer, creating the pressure that forces his choice."},{"id":"rel_isolde_mara_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_brask","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Brask sees Mara Venn as the Wardens' leading obstacle to a Cartel toll authority and works to discredit her."},{"id":"rel_tobin_isolde_resistance","source_character_id":"chr_tobin_harrow","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_brask","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tobin Harrow resists Isolde Brask's grain levy on The Hollow, setting the Hollow Circle against the Cartel."},{"id":"rel_lysa_mara_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_lysa_orrin","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Mara Venn guides Lysa Orrin from theory into field inspection, and Lysa's charts give Mara the evidence of sabotage."},{"id":"rel_tobin_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_tobin_harrow","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tobin Harrow pledges the Hollow Circle's grain and labour to Mara Venn's repair effort after meeting her at Emberroost."}]}
