toll authority over every skybridge.","flaw":"Believes everything and everyone has a price, so she fatally underestimates principled people.","internal_conflict":"She sees herself as the archipelago's stabiliser but knows her policies deepen its suffering.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist her tolls and her grain levy, threatening to unite against her.","arc":"Starts as a confident monopolist exploiting the crisis. When Joren defies her and the Wardens and Hollow Circle refuse her levy together, her leverage collapses. She ends stripped of the toll authority, forced to accept a shared charter and facing the cost of her own certainty.","personality_traits":["composed","calculating","patient","imperious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Mastery","description":"Tracks debts and wind-debt obligations across the whole archipelago.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Leverage Network","description":"Commands loyalty through the debts she holds over captains and merchants.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_harrow","name":"Tobin Harrow","description":"A broad, soft-spoken Hollow Circle miller in his fifties with flour-dusted hands and a bad knee, from The Hollow. He survived the Great Calm as a boy and remembers the hunger. He is the trusted voice of the farming isle's windmill cooperatives.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep the archipelago fed and his people free from the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Organise the Hollow Circle to withhold grain from the levy and open independent shipments through the repaired bridges.","flaw":"Avoids confrontation and hoards his doubts until they become crises.","internal_conflict":"He wants to stay neutral and safe but knows neutrality starves his neighbours.","external_conflict":"Isolde's Cartel levy threatens to strip The Hollow's granaries during the crisis.","arc":"Starts as a quiet miller who avoids taking sides. When the Cartel levy leaves The Hollow's granaries nearly empty, he travels to Emberroost and stands with Mara before the Wardens. He ends as an outspoken leader who commits the Hollow Circle to the alliance.","personality_traits":["gentle","patient","wary","resilient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Sense","description":"Judges harvest quality, storage and supply needs across isles.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Community Trust","description":"Farmers across several isles listen to him.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_lysa_orrin","name":"Lysa Orrin","description":"A young cartographer-scholar at Silverspine Academy, slight and ink-stained, with a habit of sketching maps on her sleeves. She is brilliant but sheltered, having studied skybridge charts far more than she has crossed them.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that charting the drift can predict and prevent bridge failures.","goal":"Trace the sabotage by matching altered bridge charts to the failed junctions.","flaw":"Naive and overconfident in her models, she ignores field evidence that contradicts them.","internal_conflict":"She yearns to do real work in the field but fears her theories will fail when tested.","external_conflict":"Academy elders and the Cartel pressure her to keep the altered charts quiet.","arc":"Starts as a theory-bound scholar who trusts her models over people. After her predicted-safe route fails and Mara's field inspection proves her wrong, she works beside Mara. She ends by publishing the tampered charts that expose the sabotage, having learned to test theory against reality.","personality_traits":["brilliant","earnest","sheltered","curious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Charting","description":"Models the shifting skybridge network and predicts drift patterns.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_joren_uneasy_allies","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_joren_kaul","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Venn and Joren Kaul begin as wary adversaries, Warden against Cartel pilot, and grow into allies as they survive the Mistral span together."},{"id":"rel_isolde_joren_master","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_brask","target_character_id":"chr_joren_kaul","relationship_type":"employer","description":"Isolde Brask holds Joren Kaul's family wind-debt and orders him to profiteer, creating the pressure that forces his choice."},{"id":"rel_isolde_mara_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_brask","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Brask sees Mara Venn as the Wardens' leading obstacle to a Cartel toll authority and works to discredit her."},{"id":"rel_tobin_isolde_resistance","source_character_id":"chr_tobin_harrow","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_brask","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tobin Harrow resists Isolde Brask's grain levy on The Hollow, setting the Hollow Circle against the Cartel."},{"id":"rel_lysa_mara_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","target_character_id":"chr_lysa_orrin","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Mara Venn guides Lysa Orrin from theory into field inspection, and Lysa's charts give Mara the evidence of sabotage."},{"id":"rel_tobin_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_tobin_harrow","target_character_id":"chr_mara_venn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tobin Harrow pledges the Hollow Circle's grain and labour to Mara Venn's repair effort after meeting her at Emberroost."}]}
