[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_maren_voss","name":"Maren Voss","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered Bridge Warden engineer in her late thirties, born on Emberroost to a family of cable-braiders. She has calloused hands, a close-cropped grey-streaked braid, and a soot-stained leather coat. She inspects the cloudstone cables that hold the realm together and has lately found fraying that no repair seems to stop.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges from failing, because her brother died when a bridge gave way during her apprenticeship.","goal":"Find the cause of the spreading cable failures and secure the old wards on the main skybridges before the next season's crossings.","flaw":"She trusts only her own work and refuses to delegate or share findings, even when she is overwhelmed.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between her guilt over her brother's death and her fear that the failing wards mean the realm's prosperity rests on a lie.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls force the Wardens to cut inspection budgets, while crossings keep adding wind-debt to bridges she cannot afford to close.","arc":"Maren begins as a lone engineer who hides her inspection logs and rebuilds cables by herself at night. When a Cartel toll-driven rush of crossings overloads a half-repaired span and nearly kills a family, she is forced to confront her brother's death. She shares her logs with Silverspine's cartographers and the Hollow Circle's millers to organise a coordinated rewarding of the bridges. She ends as a leader who relies on others, having addressed her need to control everything.","personality_traits":["meticulous","stubborn","guilt-ridden","dry-humoured"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and splicing cloudstone cables inside shielded forge-pits, never using open flame elsewhere.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Stress Reading","description":"Can judge a cable's remaining strength by touch and sound.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_tal","name":"Corvin Tal","role":"antagonist","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel merchant prince in his fifties, with rings on every finger and a velvet coat. He runs the busiest berths at Mistral Docks and has built his fortune on tolls and shipping lanes. He believes that strict control of trade is what keeps the realm prosperous.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's permanent hold on all inter-isle trade so that his family never faces the poverty of his youth.","goal":"Push through higher skybridge tolls and a grain levy that make the Cartel indispensable to every isle.","flaw":"His greed makes him dismiss safety warnings as bargaining tactics.","internal_conflict":"He privately suspects the wards are failing but cannot admit it without undermining the prosperity he sells.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle both resist his tolls and levy, and he is losing allies within the Cartel.","arc":"Corvin starts as a confident toll-raiser who ignores Maren's warnings. When the Grain Levy standoff leaves Mistral Docks short of grain and a bridge span nearly collapses with Cartel cargo aboard, he cannot deny the danger. He ends by funding bridge repairs and lowering tolls, acknowledging his fear of the failing wards.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","proud","anxious beneath the polish"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade Leverage","description":"Controls shipping lanes and can starve an isle of goods through contracts.","category":"social"},{"name":"Ledger Mind","description":"Remembers every debt and contract in the archipelago.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_penn","name":"Isolde Penn","role":"supporting","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy, around twenty-three, with ink-stained fingers and spectacles. She charts the shifting skybridge network and notices patterns in where bridges fail.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that careful mapping can predict failures, vindicating her mentor who was dismissed as an alarmist.","goal":"Produce a map of failure points across the skybridge network that the Wardens will act on.","flaw":"She is overconfident in her data and presents it with arrogance that alienates the people she needs.","internal_conflict":"She wants academic recognition but fears that publishing her findings will cause panic and cost lives.","external_conflict":"The Academy's board wants her charts kept quiet to protect trade relations with the Cartel.","arc":"Isolde begins by hoarding her maps for a prestigious publication. After Maren's near-disaster proves her predictions right, she chooses to hand the charts directly to the Wardens and the Hollow Circle rather than wait for acclaim. She ends as a humbler collaborator who values being useful over being credited.","personality_traits":["brilliant","impatient","idealistic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Failure Cartography","description":"Maps drift patterns and bridge stress to predict failures.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_haldane","name":"Bram Haldane","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered miller of the Hollow Circle in his forties, with flour-dusted forearms and a booming laugh. He runs the largest windmill on The Hollow and speaks for the farmers in the Grain Levy dispute.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect his community from the Cartel levy, as the Great Calm taught the Hollow to survive on its own.","goal":"Defeat the Grain Levy and keep grain shipments flowing on fair terms.","flaw":"He holds grudges and refuses to negotiate with anyone tied to the Cartel.","internal_conflict":"He wants to stay out of politics yet is increasingly pulled to lead the Circle.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents threaten to cut off his access to the skybridges, so he owes wind-debt he cannot repay in goods.","arc":"Bram starts out refusing any deal with the Cartel or its sympathisers. When a collapsing span blocks grain shipments and his debt comes due, he accepts Maren's proposal to negotiate with Corvin directly. He ends as a pragmatic leader who can bargain without surrendering his community's independence.","personality_traits":["warm","stubborn","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Mastery","description":"Keeps the windmills running through storms and calms.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_corvin_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_tal","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Voss blames Corvin Tal's tolls for the overloaded bridges and the Warden budget cuts, while Corvin sees her warnings as obstruction, fuelling the Toll War."},{"id":"rel_corvin_bram_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_tal","target_character_id":"chr_bram_haldane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Tal imposes the Grain Levy on Bram Haldane's mills, and Bram refuses to yield, escalating the dispute."},{"id":"rel_isolde_maren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_penn","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Penn supplies failure maps to Maren Voss, though her arrogance and Maren's secrecy strain their cooperation."},{"id":"rel_bram_maren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_bram_haldane","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Bram Haldane distrusts the Wardens but sides with Maren Voss against the Cartel's levy and tolls, a fragile alliance."}]}
</Output>
