{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_maren_kolvash","name":"Maren Kolvash","role":"protagonist","description":"A lean, soft-spoken Bridge Warden engineer in her late thirties, born on Emberroost to a family of cable-braiders. Her palms are scarred from decades of cloudstone fibre, and she wears a grey warden's coat patched at the elbows. After years inspecting skybridges, she keeps a private notebook of strange dreams she has had since the colony's dreamstone was first unearthed.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"She wants to prove the shared dreams are not a danger, because her late brother's final dream is the only place she can still hear his voice.","goal":"Trace the source of the dreamstone's projections and secure the stone before the Cartel can seize it.","flaw":"She clings to comforting illusions and ignores evidence that contradicts them.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between her duty to protect the colony from the stone and her craving to keep dreaming of her brother.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants to control the dreamstone and press her to hand over her survey data, while the Wardens' toll dispute leaves her short of support.","arc":"Maren begins by hiding her dependence on the shared dream of her brother and dismissing warnings about the stone. During a skybridge inspection she sees the dream draw an entire crew of Wardens off a span, and she realises the stone is feeding on longing. She chooses to wake the colony by sealing the stone in a shielded forge-pit, giving up her last dream of her brother and ending the story willing to grieve in the waking world.","personality_traits":["methodical","wistful","stubborn","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Reading","description":"She can judge the tension and fatigue of a cloudstone cable by touch and sound.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Dream Lucidity","description":"Her long exposure to the dreamstone lets her stay partly aware while inside the shared dream.","category":"supernatural"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_vask","name":"Oren Vask","role":"antagonist","description":"A broad, immaculately dressed Drift Cartel factor in his fifties, stationed at Mistral Docks. He wears rings of polished basalt and speaks in a slow, courteous voice. He rose from a deckhand to a trade lord by reading what people want and selling it back to them.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"He sees the dreamstone as the ultimate monopoly, a product everyone in the archipelago will pay a wind-debt to experience.","goal":"Take control of the dreamstone and license access to the shared dreams across every isle.","flaw":"He treats every person and every wonder as a commodity to be priced.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears that his own dreams are empty and that the stone shows he has nothing he truly wants.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist Cartel levies, and Maren's survey control blocks his claim to the stone.","arc":"Oren starts out certain that the stone is a mere asset he can price. When the Grain Levy dispute erupts and the Hollow Circle's members refuse to sell their dreams, he enters the dream himself and sees only a vacant, ledger-filled void. He ends by hoarding the stone more desperately, but loses the loyalty of his own crew, who see his emptiness.","personality_traits":["courteous","calculating","insecure","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Market Sense","description":"He reads the needs and weaknesses of others and turns them into leverage in negotiation.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_ryle","name":"Tamsin Ryle","role":"supporting","description":"A wiry young cartographer at Silverspine Academy, barely twenty-three, with ink-stained fingers and cropped red hair. She charts shifting skybridge routes and has started mapping where the shared dreams are strongest.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"She wants to be the first scholar to map the dream's reach, earning a place among the Academy's masters.","goal":"Produce a complete chart of the dream's spread across the isles.","flaw":"She is reckless about risk when data is within reach.","internal_conflict":"She wants recognition but fears her ambition is putting others in danger.","external_conflict":"The Academy elders deny her funding, and the Cartel offers to buy her maps.","arc":"Tamsin begins as an eager mapmaker who will trade her charts to anyone for support. After the Cartel uses her map to find the stone's chamber, she realises her work has exposed the colony. She chooses to burn the original plates in a shielded forge-pit and publicly share a corrected chart that points away from the stone, ending as a more careful scholar.","personality_traits":["eager","clever","impulsive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"She charts shifting bridge networks quickly and accurately.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_hollis","name":"Bram Hollis","role":"supporting","description":"A heavyset miller in his sixties from The Hollow, with flour-dusted forearms and a booming laugh. He was a young man during the Great Calm and still stockpiles grain against hard times. He has begun to hear the dream in the creak of his windmill.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"He wants to protect his neighbours' independence, born from the self-reliance the Great Calm taught him.","goal":"Keep the Hollow Circle out of Cartel debt and out of the dream's grip.","flaw":"He distrusts outsiders so strongly that he rejects help even when it is offered honestly.","internal_conflict":"He is proud of his self-reliance yet knows the Hollow cannot resist the Cartel levy alone.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy threatens to bankrupt the Hollow, and its agents are courting his neighbours.","arc":"Bram starts by refusing every outside offer. When the Grain Levy forces his village to the brink and Maren arrives with a plan to seal the stone, he must choose between pride and survival. He accepts her help and organises the millers to supply the Wardens, ending as a bridge between the Circle and the Wardens.","personality_traits":["gruff","loyal","proud","generous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Craft","description":"He can read wind currents and keep the mills grinding in poor weather.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_oren_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_maren_kolvash","target_character_id":"chr_oren_vask","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Maren Kolvash opposes Oren Vask because he wants to seize the dreamstone she is trying to seal, and the Toll War keeps their factions in open conflict."},{"id":"rel_oren_tamsin_patron","source_character_id":"chr_oren_vask","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_ryle","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Oren Vask lures Tamsin Ryle with offers to buy her charts, using her ambition to locate the stone and undermining Maren's secrecy."},{"id":"rel_maren_tamsin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_maren_kolvash","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_ryle","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Maren Kolvash guides Tamsin Ryle in judging skybridge risks, but Tamsin's reckless mapping strains their trust."},{"id":"rel_bram_oren_levy","source_character_id":"chr_bram_hollis","target_character_id":"chr_oren_vask","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Bram Hollis resists Oren Vask's Grain Levy, which Oren uses to pressure the Hollow Circle into surrendering its dreamers."},{"id":"rel_bram_maren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_bram_hollis","target_character_id":"chr_maren_kolvash","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Bram Hollis grudgingly allies with Maren Kolvash against the Cartel, supplying grain and workers for her plan to seal the stone."}]}
</Output>
