[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_veln","name":"Mara Veln","description":"A sharp-tongued Bridge Warden inspector in her late thirties, Mara grew up in the cable sheds of Emberroost, braiding cloudstone beside her father until a frayed span took his life. She wears a soot-stained warden's coat, keeps a notched measuring rod at her belt, and greets every disaster with dry, weary sarcasm. She is now posted to Silverspine Academy to audit the skybridge charts.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To make sure no other family loses someone to a bridge that was neglected for profit.","goal":"Prove that falsified survey charts are hiding weakened skybridge spans, and get them publicly corrected.","flaw":"Uses sarcasm and solitude to keep people at arm's length, so she rarely shares evidence or asks for help.","internal_conflict":"She believes trusting anyone means risking another loss, yet she cannot expose the forgery alone.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls and the Toll War push the Wardens to ignore bridge defects that would cut shipping.","arc":"Mara begins as a lone inspector who hoards her findings and mocks her colleagues. Pursuing the Toll War, she discovers a forged chart on a frayed skybridge and, rather than fixing it quietly herself, she chooses to share the proof with Dorrin Ashk and the Academy's cartographers. She ends as a warden who builds a coalition and accepts shared responsibility.","personality_traits":["sarcastic","vigilant","stubborn","dry-witted","secretly guilt-ridden"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Sense","description":"Judges the tension and fatigue of a cloudstone cable by touch and sound.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Span Auditing","description":"Spots inconsistencies in survey charts and load records.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_dorrin_ashk","name":"Dorrin Ashk","description":"A rumpled, middle-aged senior cartographer at Silverspine Academy with ink-stained cuffs and a habit of talking to his maps. He has charted the shifting skybridge network for twenty years and takes quiet pride in its accuracy, which makes the discovery of tampering especially painful for him.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To preserve the integrity of the Academy's charts as a record that every traveller can trust.","goal":"Find out who altered the Academy's skybridge survey charts and restore the original records.","flaw":"Conflict-averse, he delays confrontations and rationalises suspicious requests as clerical errors.","internal_conflict":"His loyalty to the Academy's reputation clashes with the growing evidence that someone inside has been bribed.","external_conflict":"Cartel-funded patrons pressure the Academy to approve chart revisions that favour their shipping lanes.","arc":"Dorrin starts as a cautious scholar who explains away odd chart revisions. When Mara shows him a forged span record that contradicts his own originals, he must choose between the Academy's reputation and the truth. He testifies openly and ends as a man willing to risk his standing to defend the record.","personality_traits":["meticulous","gentle","anxious","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Network Cartography","description":"Reconstructs the drifting skybridge network from fragmentary survey data.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sable_quill","name":"Sable Quill","description":"A polished Drift Cartel factor in her forties, Sable rose from Mistral Docks dockhand to merchant-prince's right hand. She dresses in storm-grey silk, speaks softly, and treats every bridge toll as an elegant equation. She believes the Cartel keeps the isles alive.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's lasting dominance so she never returns to the poverty of the docks.","goal":"Keep shipping lanes open and tolls rising by suppressing evidence that key skybridge spans are unsafe.","flaw":"Her pride makes her treat any opposition as a personal insult, and she overreaches to win quickly.","internal_conflict":"She knows a failing span could kill the very traders she claims to protect, but she cannot admit the risk without losing her position.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle both resist the Cartel's tolls and Grain Levy, threatening her profits.","arc":"Sable begins as a confident fixer who bribes clerks to alter charts. When Mara's evidence and the Hollow Circle's resistance in the Grain Levy dispute corner her, she doubles down and bribes more people, which exposes her. She ends discredited, forced to face that her pride caused the danger she denied.","personality_traits":["calculating","polite","proud","ruthless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Toll Negotiation","description":"Bends merchants and officials to her terms through leverage and charm.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_reeve","name":"Tobin Reeve","description":"A broad-shouldered young miller from The Hollow with flour-dusted hair and an easy laugh. He represents his village in the Hollow Circle and has been dragged into inter-isle politics by the Cartel's grain levy.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect his village's livelihood and keep grain affordable for the isles.","goal":"Get the Cartel's grain levy lifted or reduced through a public hearing.","flaw":"Hot-tempered and quick to make promises he cannot keep.","internal_conflict":"He wants peace for his village but is tempted to answer the Cartel with sabotage.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy threatens to bankrupt Hollow Circle millers within a season, and wind-debt keeps them tied to Cartel shipping.","arc":"Tobin begins as a furious miller ready to sabotage Cartel cargo. After Mara shows him that Sable's levy relies on the same suspect charts, he chooses to testify rather than sabotage. He ends as a patient advocate who wins his village a hearing.","personality_traits":["warm","impulsive","loyal","blunt"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Reckoning","description":"Quickly estimates harvests, yields and fair prices.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_sable_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Mara Veln is investigating Sable Quill's suppression of unsafe skybridge records, and Sable regards Mara as a threat to the Cartel's toll revenue."},{"id":"rel_mara_dorrin_colleagues","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_dorrin_ashk","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Veln reluctantly relies on Dorrin Ashk's expertise to verify the forged charts, while his hesitation frustrates her."},{"id":"rel_sable_dorrin_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","target_character_id":"chr_dorrin_ashk","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sable Quill pressures Dorrin Ashk through Cartel-funded patrons to approve altered charts, forcing him to choose between the Academy and the truth."},{"id":"rel_tobin_sable_levy","source_character_id":"chr_tobin_reeve","target_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tobin Reeve opposes Sable Quill's Grain Levy, which threatens to ruin the millers of The Hollow."},{"id":"rel_tobin_mara_allies","source_character_id":"chr_tobin_reeve","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tobin Reeve and Mara Veln form a wary alliance, trading Mara's chart evidence for Tobin's testimony against the Cartel."}]}
</Output>
