s open and tolls rising by suppressing evidence that key skybridge spans are unsafe.","flaw":"Her pride makes her treat any opposition as a personal insult, and she overreaches to win quickly.","internal_conflict":"She knows a failing span could kill the very traders she claims to protect, but she cannot admit the risk without losing her position.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle both resist the Cartel's tolls and Grain Levy, threatening her profits.","arc":"Sable begins as a confident fixer who bribes clerks to alter charts. When Mara's evidence and the Hollow Circle's resistance in the Grain Levy dispute corner her, she doubles down and bribes more people, which exposes her. She ends discredited, forced to face that her pride caused the danger she denied.","personality_traits":["calculating","polite","proud","ruthless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Toll Negotiation","description":"Bends merchants and officials to her terms through leverage and charm.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_reeve","name":"Tobin Reeve","description":"A broad-shouldered young miller from The Hollow with flour-dusted hair and an easy laugh. He represents his village in the Hollow Circle and has been dragged into inter-isle politics by the Cartel's grain levy.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect his village's livelihood and keep grain affordable for the isles.","goal":"Get the Cartel's grain levy lifted or reduced through a public hearing.","flaw":"Hot-tempered and quick to make promises he cannot keep.","internal_conflict":"He wants peace for his village but is tempted to answer the Cartel with sabotage.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy threatens to bankrupt Hollow Circle millers within a season, and wind-debt keeps them tied to Cartel shipping.","arc":"Tobin begins as a furious miller ready to sabotage Cartel cargo. After Mara shows him that Sable's levy relies on the same suspect charts, he chooses to testify rather than sabotage. He ends as a patient advocate who wins his village a hearing.","personality_traits":["warm","impulsive","loyal","blunt"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Reckoning","description":"Quickly estimates harvests, yields and fair prices.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_sable_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Mara Veln is investigating Sable Quill's suppression of unsafe skybridge records, and Sable regards Mara as a threat to the Cartel's toll revenue."},{"id":"rel_mara_dorrin_colleagues","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_dorrin_ashk","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Veln reluctantly relies on Dorrin Ashk's expertise to verify the forged charts, while his hesitation frustrates her."},{"id":"rel_sable_dorrin_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","target_character_id":"chr_dorrin_ashk","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sable Quill pressures Dorrin Ashk through Cartel-funded patrons to approve altered charts, forcing him to choose between the Academy and the truth."},{"id":"rel_tobin_sable_levy","source_character_id":"chr_tobin_reeve","target_character_id":"chr_sable_quill","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tobin Reeve opposes Sable Quill's Grain Levy, which threatens to ruin the millers of The Hollow."},{"id":"rel_tobin_mara_allies","source_character_id":"chr_tobin_reeve","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tobin Reeve and Mara Veln form a wary alliance, trading Mara's chart evidence for Tobin's testimony against the Cartel."}]}
