{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_odette_marsh","name":"Odette Marsh","description":"A sharp-eyed retired Silverspine cartographer in her sixties, with silver hair pinned under a faded blue scarf and ink-stained fingers. She charted skybridge routes for decades and now accepts weekend invitations to country manors for the gossip and the tea. Her small frame and gentle manner hide a meticulous memory for detail.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"She wants to prove her mind is still as sharp as her reputation claims, after colleagues quietly retired her.","goal":"Identify the murderer among the manor guests before the skybridge to the mainland is repaired and the culprit can leave.","flaw":"She is a compulsive meddler who cannot let a puzzle alone, even when poking at it endangers others.","internal_conflict":"She fears her age has dulled her judgment, yet she cannot bring herself to accept help from others.","external_conflict":"The guests close ranks against her questions, and the Cartel-aligned host's staff try to steer her away from the study where the victim was found.","arc":"Starts as a doubtful, solitary retiree who dismisses her own hunches. When she discovers that the victim's ledger of unpaid wind-debts was altered, she must choose between confronting the culprit alone or trusting Tobias Finch with her evidence. She shares her findings, accepts his help, and ends confident and collaborative, no longer needing to prove herself alone.","personality_traits":["observant","witty","stubborn","kindly"],"abilities":[{"name":"Photographic Route Memory","description":"She can recall the layout of any chart or room she has seen once, and notices what has been moved.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Disarming Charm","description":"Her grandmotherly manner coaxes confidences from wary guests.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_finch","name":"Tobias Finch","description":"A broad-shouldered young Hollow miller in his late twenties, with flour-dusted forearms and an awkward, apologetic smile. He was invited to the manor to negotiate a grain levy settlement and wears a borrowed jacket that does not quite fit.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"He wants to protect his village from being ruined by the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Secure a written levy exemption from the host's estate before the weekend ends.","flaw":"He is painfully naive and trusts anyone who is polite to him.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between his duty to the Hollow Circle and a growing sense that the exemption is being bought with his silence.","external_conflict":"Because he argued loudly with the victim over the levy, the other guests suspect him of the murder.","arc":"Begins as a trusting, easily led negotiator under suspicion. When Odette shows him that the host's secretary has been forging levy papers, he realises his politeness has been used against him. He testifies openly against the forger and ends as a shrewder, more assertive advocate for his village.","personality_traits":["earnest","gullible","loyal","gentle"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Accounting","description":"He can estimate shipment weights and spot falsified tallies at a glance.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Steady Strength","description":"Years at the mill let him haul heavy loads without tiring.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_lucian_vane","name":"Lucian Vane","description":"A polished Mistral Docks merchant prince in his fifties, with slicked dark hair, rings on every finger and a velvet voice. He holds the manor deed as collateral and rules the guest list with practiced hospitality.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"He is determined to keep his Cartel shipping monopoly intact and hide the debts that threaten to expose him.","goal":"Destroy the victim's ledger and pin the blame on a convenient outsider.","flaw":"His arrogance makes him certain no one would dare question him.","internal_conflict":"He despises the dishonesty his position requires but has built his whole identity on it.","external_conflict":"The Toll War has soured his standing with the Wardens, and the victim's evidence could hand them the leverage they need.","arc":"Starts as a smug, unshakable host. When Odette notices the ledger's altered wind-debt entries, his control slips and he tries to frame Tobias. His arrogance leads him to mishandle the evidence, and he ends exposed and stripped of his standing.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","controlling"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"He smooths over any awkward question with gracious deflection.","category":"social"},{"name":"Trade Network","description":"He can call on Cartel agents across the isles to carry messages or favours.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_marguerite_quill","name":"Marguerite Quill","description":"A composed Emberroost cable-braider turned Warden inspector in her forties, with burn-scarred hands, cropped grey-streaked hair and a severe grey coat. She came to inspect the manor's skybridge anchor and was invited to stay the weekend.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"She wants to prove that Cartel tolls are being skimmed rather than spent on bridge upkeep.","goal":"Obtain the victim's toll records and carry them back to the Wardens.","flaw":"Her rigid sense of duty makes her withhold information, even from potential allies.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between her loyalty to the Wardens' rules and her suspicion that the Wardens' own leadership took Cartel payments.","external_conflict":"Lucian Vane's staff watch her movements, and the missing toll records make her the prime suspect for theft.","arc":"Begins as a guarded, by-the-book inspector hiding her purpose. When the manor's bridge anchor is found tampered with, she chooses to reveal her mission to Odette instead of reporting only to the Wardens. She ends as a more open, flexible ally who values justice over procedure.","personality_traits":["disciplined","secretive","blunt","principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Anchor Inspection","description":"She can read stress, wear, and tampering on a cloudstone cable or anchor at a glance.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Shielded Forge Craft","description":"She is trained to work cloudstone safely using shielded forge-pits only.","category":"technological"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_odette_tobias_ally","source_character_id":"chr_odette_marsh","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_finch","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Odette Marsh takes the suspected Tobias Finch under her wing, recognising his innocence and relying on his grain-ledger skills to expose the forgery."},{"id":"rel_lucian_odette_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_lucian_vane","target_character_id":"chr_odette_marsh","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Lucian Vane sees Odette Marsh's quiet questioning as a threat and works to mislead and isolate her, amplifying the conflict at the manor."},{"id":"rel_lucian_tobias_antagonist","source_character_id":"chr_lucian_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_finch","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Lucian Vane exploits Tobias Finch's trust over the grain levy and tries to frame him for the murder to protect Cartel interests."},{"id":"rel_marguerite_lucian_rival","source_character_id":"chr_marguerite_quill","target_character_id":"chr_lucian_vane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marguerite Quill suspects Lucian Vane of skimming Cartel toll money meant for bridge upkeep, deepening the Toll War tension between them."},{"id":"rel_marguerite_odette_ally","source_character_id":"chr_marguerite_quill","target_character_id":"chr_odette_marsh","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Marguerite Quill, a fellow bridge professional, gradually shares her inspection findings with Odette Marsh, forming a cautious alliance to expose the culprit."}]}
