{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kael_voss","name":"Kael Voss","description":"A weathered former skyship corsair in his late thirties, Kael spent fifteen years raiding Cartel cargo lanes above Mistral Docks before a pardon bound him to honest work. He has a rope-scarred left forearm, close-cropped salt-grey hair, and a patched coat of storm-blue canvas. He now takes courier jobs and carries the guilt of the crews he left behind.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":null,"motivation":"To earn back a name that is not synonymous with theft and prove his pardon was deserved.","goal":"Recover the stolen skybridge chart and return it to its rightful keepers.","flaw":"Reflexive recklessness: he leaps into daring plans without counting who pays for them.","internal_conflict":"He fears the honest man he is becoming is a costume, and that the old corsair is who he really is.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants the map for itself and holds his pardon over him, while Bridge Wardens suspect him of the theft.","arc":"Kael starts as a pardoned rogue who solves problems with bravado. When he is offered the chance to sell the recovered map to the Cartel to clear his debts and he sees the Toll War would worsen, he chooses to hand it to the Wardens at personal cost. He ends as a man who accepts responsibility over glory.","personality_traits":["bold","wry","guilt-ridden","loyal","impulsive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windrunner Piloting","description":"Reads wind currents to steer small skiffs through storm lanes and between drifting isles.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Underworld Contacts","description":"Knows smugglers and dockhands who trade in rumours about stolen goods.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_marrow","name":"Isolde Marrow","description":"A sharp-eyed senior cartographer at Silverspine Academy, in her fifties, with ink-stained fingers, spectacles on a brass chain, and a rigid, upright bearing. She charted the skybridge network for decades and believes maps belong to everyone who must cross the sky.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridge charts in public hands so no faction can strand the isles by controlling routes.","goal":"Have the stolen map recovered and its routes verified before the next season of drift.","flaw":"Rigid distrust of anyone with a criminal past, which makes her dismiss useful allies.","internal_conflict":"She loves knowledge freely shared but secretly guards her own discoveries out of pride.","external_conflict":"Academy superiors pressure her to blame Kael, and the Cartel tries to buy her copies of the charts.","arc":"Isolde begins by refusing to work with ex-pirates. After Kael's information on a Cartel shipment proves true and saves a bridge crossing, she shares her private survey notes with him. She ends willing to judge people by deeds rather than records.","personality_traits":["meticulous","proud","principled","stern"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Plots shifting skybridge routes and predicts how drift will alter them.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_dorian_vale","name":"Dorian Vale","description":"A silver-tongued Cartel merchant prince in his forties, with rings on every finger, a velvet coat dyed deep crimson, and a smile that never reaches his eyes. He rose through the Cartel after the signing of its charter and views control of trade lanes as destiny.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the full chart of skybridges so the Cartel can set tolls on every crossing without rival.","goal":"Seize the stolen map before the Wardens do and use it to extend the Cartel's toll monopoly.","flaw":"Overconfidence that everyone has a price, so he underestimates people who refuse to be bought.","internal_conflict":"He resents the cartel elders who treat him as a tool and craves their recognition he may never earn.","external_conflict":"The Toll War and the Grain Levy have turned the Wardens and the Hollow Circle against him, threatening his standing.","arc":"Dorian starts certain that wealth can acquire anything. When Kael refuses his bribe and the Hollow Circle's resistance to the levy exposes his overreach before the Cartel council, he loses his position. He ends diminished and forced to reckon with his dependence on others' approval.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","ambitious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade Leverage","description":"Uses debts and wind-debt obligations to compel favours from captains and merchants.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_brae","name":"Tamsin Brae","description":"A young Hollow Circle miller in her early twenties, broad-shouldered with flour-dusted braids and a quiet, steady gaze. She leads her isle's resistance to the grain levy and ferries sacks aboard a battered skiff.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect her community from Cartel levies that would leave her neighbours hungry.","goal":"Defeat the grain levy by proving the Cartel's maneuvers publicly.","flaw":"Stubborn pride makes her refuse help even when she is outmatched.","internal_conflict":"She wants to stay and tend the mills but dreams of a wider world beyond the Hollow.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents threaten her family's shipping contracts and intimidate other millers into paying.","arc":"Tamsin begins as a reluctant local who insists on fighting alone. When Kael ferries her evidence of the levy to the Wardens at Emberroost, she accepts allies and testifies publicly. She ends as a recognised voice for her people willing to leave the Hollow when needed.","personality_traits":["steadfast","humble","stubborn","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Engineering","description":"Repairs and tunes windmills and grain machinery under pressure.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_ostrander","name":"Bram Ostrander","description":"A burly Bridge Warden engineer at Emberroost, grey-bearded and soot-streaked, who has braided cloudstone cables for thirty years. He wears a leather apron and speaks slowly, with great care.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep every skybridge safe so no crossing ends in tragedy like the one that took his brother.","goal":"Hold the Wardens' bridges together despite Cartel tolls straining their funds.","flaw":"Inflexible caution that delays decisions until opportunities pass.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between his oath to remain neutral and his anger at the Cartel's greed.","external_conflict":"Rising tolls cut his repair budget and force him to ration cable.","arc":"Bram begins by refusing to act beyond his oath. When Kael presents the recovered map showing a failing span, Bram breaks protocol to dispatch crews before approval. He ends as a leader willing to act decisively when lives are at stake.","personality_traits":["patient","dutiful","gruff","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Braids and repairs skybridge cables inside shielded forge-pits without open flame outside them.","category":"technological"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_kael_dorian_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_kael_voss","target_character_id":"chr_dorian_vale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Kael Voss raided Dorian Vale's cargo lanes for years, and Dorian now holds Kael's pardon as leverage to force him to deliver the map, making them bitter adversaries."},{"id":"rel_dorian_kael_coerce","source_character_id":"chr_dorian_vale","target_character_id":"chr_kael_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Dorian Vale tries to coerce and bribe Kael Voss into handing over the map, amplifying Kael's temptation to return to old habits."},{"id":