[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_marra_venn","name":"Marra Venn","description":"A weathered caravan-mistress in her late forties who has led her family's skybridge caravan from Mistral Docks for twenty years. She has sun-creased skin, a braid streaked with grey, and a coat patched with cloudstone-thread from every isle she has crossed. She inherited the caravan and its mounting wind-debts from her father.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep her family's caravan and its hired crew together and fed through the lean seasons.","goal":"Carry a full load of Hollow grain across the Emberroost bridges and clear the caravan's wind-debt before the season ends.","flaw":"She is stubbornly self-reliant and refuses to share burdens or accept help.","internal_conflict":"She wants to be a neutral trader but feels loyalty to the crew and drivers who are caught in the Toll War.","external_conflict":"Cartel tolls and the Grain Levy squeeze her routes, and both the Cartel and the Wardens pressure her to carry cargo for their side.","arc":"Marra begins as a proud loner who hoards decisions and debt. When the Grain Levy lets Cartel agents seize her grain at the Mistral Docks, she chooses to ask the Hollow Circle and a Warden engineer for help and pledges her labour to repair a bridge. She ends as a leader who shares risk and has built a trusted shared route.","personality_traits":["resourceful","warm","stubborn","dry-humoured"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind Reading","description":"Reads gusts and drift patterns to time skybridge crossings safely.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Hard Bargaining","description":"Negotiates tolls and wind-debt terms with merchants and officials.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_ashgrove","name":"Tobin Ashgrove","description":"A young miller's son from The Hollow, lanky and freckled, who joins the caravan as a driver to escape the Grain Levy's grip on his family. He wears flour-dusted work clothes and carries a hand-carved windmill charm.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To save his family's mill from ruin under the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Deliver his village's grain safely to market and bring back coin to pay the levy.","flaw":"He is naive and quick to trust anyone who is friendly.","internal_conflict":"He longs to see the wider archipelago but feels guilty for leaving his family behind.","external_conflict":"Cartel collectors target Hollow shipments, and he is pursued by a levy enforcer.","arc":"Tobin starts as a trusting youth who hands his family's ledger to a smiling Cartel clerk. When the clerk takes the grain through the Grain Levy, he learns to verify contracts and rallies Hollow Circle farmers to a joint shipment. He ends as a cautious, confident negotiator for his village.","personality_traits":["earnest","curious","homesick","optimistic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Sense","description":"Judges the quality and moisture of grain by touch and smell.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_selene_ironbraid","name":"Selene Ironbraid","description":"A senior Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, stern and broad-shouldered, with scarred hands from braiding cloudstone cable. She carries a toolkit and a ledger of bridge inspections.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep every skybridge sound so no traveller falls.","goal":"Inspect and repair the failing bridges on the caravan's route before the next storm.","flaw":"She is rigid and distrusts merchants, assuming all of them are greedy.","internal_conflict":"She believes in service to all but resents the traders whose tolls burden the Wardens.","external_conflict":"The Toll War cuts the Wardens' funding and the Cartel obstructs her repairs.","arc":"Selene begins by treating Marra's caravan as an enemy of the Wardens. When a cable frays mid-crossing and Marra's crew holds the line without any open flame near the bridge, she sees merchants as allies. She ends by co-designing a fair toll-for-labour exchange with the caravan.","personality_traits":["disciplined","blunt","meticulous","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Braids and splices cloudstone cable to repair skybridges.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Structural Insight","description":"Spots stress faults in a bridge by sight and sound.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_dray","name":"Corvin Dray","description":"A smooth-spoken Drift Cartel factor at Mistral Docks, in his fifties, with rings on every finger and a ledger he never lets out of reach. He rose from a dockhand and now enforces the grain levy.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure his seat among the Cartel's merchant princes and never be poor again.","goal":"Collect the Grain Levy in full and force the caravan to carry Cartel cargo.","flaw":"Greed and fear of losing status make him ruthless with those weaker than him.","internal_conflict":"He remembers his dockhand past and secretly sympathises with small traders but suppresses it.","external_conflict":"Rival princes and the Wardens' resistance threaten his position as the Toll War escalates.","arc":"Corvin starts as a levy enforcer who crushes small traders for status. When Marra's shared route exposes his falsified levy tallies to the Cartel's own princes, he must choose between covering up and confessing. He ends by quietly cancelling the levy on the Hollow shipments, trading his rank for a measure of redemption.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","ambitious","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Craft","description":"Manipulates accounts and contract terms to the Cartel's advantage.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ilsa_quillfern","name":"Ilsa Quillfern","description":"A young cartographer from Silverspine Academy, ink-stained and bespectacled, who joins the caravan to chart the shifting skybridge network. She keeps a leather folio of half-finished maps.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To complete the first accurate chart of the drifting skybridges.","goal":"Map a safe route through the Toll War zones for the caravan.","flaw":"She is absent-minded and puts her maps ahead of the safety of her companions.","internal_conflict":"She wants scholarly neutrality yet is drawn to take a side in the Toll War.","external_conflict":"Academy elders forbid sharing maps with merchants and the Cartel wants to buy her charts.","arc":"Ilsa begins as an aloof scholar who hoards her unfinished maps. When the caravan is stranded between collapsing bridges, she shares her charts openly and guides everyone out. She ends as a cartographer who publishes free route maps for the common good.","personality_traits":["curious","distracted","brilliant","idealistic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Route Charting","description":"Charts shifting skybridge routes and predicts their drift.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marra_corvin_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_marra_venn","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_dray","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marra Venn and Corvin Dray are rivals: Corvin uses the Cartel's levy and tolls to pressure Marra into carrying his cargo, and Marra resists him."},{"id":"rel_marra_tobin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_marra_venn","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_ashgrove","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Marra Venn mentors Tobin Ashgrove, teaching him the caravan trade while his trust in strangers keeps putting her load at risk."},{"id":"rel_selene_marra_wary","source_character_id":"chr_selene_ironbraid","target_character_id":"chr_marra_venn","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Selene Ironbraid distrusts Marra Venn as a Cartel-linked merchant, creating friction over tolls and bridge repairs until a shared crossing makes them allies."},{"id":"rel_corvin_tobin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_dray","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_ashgrove","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Dray targets Tobin Ashgrove's family mill with the Grain Levy, pitting the Cartel against the Hollow Circle."},{"id":"rel_ilsa_selene_ally","source_character_id":"chr_ilsa_quillfern","target_character_id":"chr_selene_ironbraid","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilsa Quillfern and Selene Ironbraid are Warden allies who trade bridge survey data, though Ilsa's carelessness frustrates Selene."}]}
</Output>
